WEBVTT

00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:02.156
of the word shayun,

00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:03.950
which means "something"

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.798
just like the the English word "something" --

00:02:05.798 --> 00:02:09.084
some undefined, unknown thing.

00:02:09.084 --> 00:02:10.249
Now in Arabic,

00:02:10.249 --> 00:02:11.450
we can make this definite

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.598
by adding the definite article "al."

00:02:13.598 --> 00:02:16.200
So this is al-shayun --

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.850
the unknown thing.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.153
And this is a word that appears throughout early mathematics,

00:02:21.153 --> 00:02:28.353
such as this 10th-century derivation of roots.

00:02:28.353 --> 00:02:30.863
The problem for the Medieval Spanish scholars